HST Office: a tab switch shows the new tab window only once it is painted and presented (Windows).

Measured on HST5 (Windows 11, Skia) with tests/runtime/check-windows-tab-switch-flash.py, which samples a
patch grid of the screen in every frame the compositor presents (DXGI Desktop Duplication): after
hst-document-tab-switch-no-flash.patch no switch showed the desktop any more, but 1 to 3 composed frames of
nearly every tab switch inside a window (HST Office window and per-application tab windows; Writer,
Sheets, Slides, Draw, HST PDF and the Start Center, same- and cross-application) showed the new window
blank: pure white patches where both the old and the new tab show grey UI. Separate windows (one
document per window) showed none. A newly shown window is composed at once, before vcl has painted it and
Skia has presented its picture.

DocumentTabGroup::activate now shows the target window cloaked (DWMWA_CLOAK: shown, painted and presented
as usual, but not composed) while the previous tab still covers the screen. ParkIdleHdl paints it,
waits for one composition (DwmFlush), uncloaks it, waits for the composition that shows it, and only then
hides the previous tab. A switch that comes before that uncloaks the pending window first, so one window
is always on screen; shutdown and an aborted activation uncloak too. Other platforms are unchanged
(no-ops).

